WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.334
-That is hard work right there.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:05.734
-This is so heavy, man.
-Can I feel it?

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:08.501
-Yes. They told me
to never put it down,

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:11.267
because people
have been known to steal it.

00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:12.434
You know, occasionally,

00:00:12.434 --> 00:00:14.300
I'll just set it down
to talk to somebody.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:19.033
And they told me that they stole
Frances McDormand's last year.

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:22.634
So no matter what you do,
keep it on your person.

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:25.901
So, literally, on the plane
the whole time, I'm spooning...

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:28.367
I was spooning with --
-With your Oscar.

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:30.234
-Yes.
-Let me just feel it.

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:31.300
Oh, my gosh.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.033
-Yeah, it's --
-Wow. It feels great.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.567
It's a legit --
It's a great award.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.968
-It's -- Yes, it's a weight
I'm willing to carry.

00:00:36.968 --> 00:00:40.934
-Well, thank you for
making it back here.

00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:43.133
Welcome home.
-I made it back.

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:45.601
Yes, I barely made it back.
[ Laughs ]

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:49.367
-What have the last
24 hours been like for you?

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:51.400
Did you -- Have you slept?

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.000
-Oh, no, absolutely not.
-Yeah.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.200
-I did the, you know, the --
whatever they call

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.067
the exit where you, like,
just back out the room

00:00:58.067 --> 00:01:02.300
and kind of just disappear,
you know,

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.200
'cause I was wise enough to --

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.467
'Cause when you're nominated
for an Oscar

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:12.734
and it's that far in advance,
anxiety starts to set in.

00:01:12.734 --> 00:01:16.901
And, for me, I was
wise enough to figure out

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:19.234
how to distract myself
in this moment.

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:21.033
And, of course,
anyone who knows me well,

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:23.434
either on the Internet
or you personally,

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:24.934
you know that there's no

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:27.334
deejay gig
I won't ever turn down.

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:33.033
And to do the
Jay-Z/Beyoncé Gold Party

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:36.968
is one of the hardest things
ever to do in life,

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:39.100
like, to please
that many people in that --

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:43.300
-Yeah. So you purposely chose
that you're gonna deejay

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:44.934
Beyoncé's and Jay-Z's party

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:46.868
because that'll be
more pressure in your head.

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:49.634
-Oh, up until that --
Once I accepted that gig,

00:01:49.634 --> 00:01:50.701
then it was like,
"Oh, what Oscar?

00:01:50.701 --> 00:01:51.701
I don't care."

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:53.868
But, at night, I'm like, "Oh,

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:55.000
I got to pick out
the right song."

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.000
-What are they saying --
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.367
-Right. So, I...

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:59.234
-Did you end up playing
Smash Mouth?

00:02:01.667 --> 00:02:03.801
-I forgot we had a bet.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.334
I mean, I played
"Smells Like Teen Spirit,"

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:12.133
which is -- No, Jimmy and I had
a bet that my first song

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:14.534
was gonna be Smash Mouth,
"All Star,"

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:18.834
which I don't think is what
Jay-Z really wants to hear.

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:21.167
-But what if they were like,
"Oh, here comes Questlove.

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:22.334
What's he going to play?"

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:24.868
-I know no one that fronts on
"All Star."

00:02:24.868 --> 00:02:26.267
So it's like,
when you put it on,

00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:27.801
you're forced to sing it
against your will.

00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:29.868
-You have to, including Jay-Z.

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:31.133
-Exactly. So --
-He would be like...

00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:32.567
♪ Somebody once told...♪

00:02:32.567 --> 00:02:34.501
-Right.
-And he would get into it.

00:02:34.501 --> 00:02:36.834
Anyway...
-So, I'll tell you this much.

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:40.601
And there was one point where
it just became, like,

00:02:40.601 --> 00:02:44.801
a cyclone of a mosh pit.

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:48.901
And inside this mosh pit of
just jumping people,

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:52.734
I see Anna Wintour
sort of, like, in the thing.

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:56.100
-So I think --
-No way. You did well.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:59.501
-Yeah. I think that if I do
the Met Gala,

00:02:59.501 --> 00:03:01.801
then I'll start off with
Smash Mouth.

00:03:01.801 --> 00:03:03.100
-Alright, alright. Perfect.
-There you go.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:08.334
-When you're in the crowd
and they announce your name

00:03:08.334 --> 00:03:12.467
that you won and everyone
gives you a standing ovation,

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:16.300
when you're next to your mother,
what is going through your head?

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:20.067
And how -- Did you --
I mean, you got emotional,

00:03:20.067 --> 00:03:23.000
but I would have been --
I was crying in my living room.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.267
-We were the only
two people in the room.

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:28.501
Like, it was that moment
that I realized that, like,

00:03:28.501 --> 00:03:34.434
we went through so much,
like, from, you know,

00:03:34.434 --> 00:03:37.667
them sacrificing
to put me in music school,

00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:42.167
and, you know, it's like
either our bills or my future.

00:03:42.167 --> 00:03:45.868
And I just thought about
all those moments

00:03:45.868 --> 00:03:48.868
and -- You know,
and, of course, you know,

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:52.767
that happened in the cyclone of
a whole 'nother situation

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.501
with two very good
friends of mine.

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:58.133
And I really
wasn't aware of that.

00:03:58.133 --> 00:04:01.567
It's weird to say,
because, you know,

00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:03.901
they tell you ahead of time,
"This is your category."

00:04:03.901 --> 00:04:06.267
And so, in that moment,
you are either going to be

00:04:06.267 --> 00:04:09.601
full of anxiety, or, for me,
like, I've been, like,

00:04:09.601 --> 00:04:11.200
meditating for like
the last two years.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:14.400
So I do trans-med -- Actually,
Seinfeld taught me about that.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:15.534
Like --
-T.M.

00:04:15.534 --> 00:04:16.934
-Yeah, T.M.

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:19.434
And, you know, a minute --
When the commercial break was

00:04:19.434 --> 00:04:22.934
happening, I was
just in my "Mmmmm."

00:04:22.934 --> 00:04:24.634
So, when I opened my eyes,
I didn't realize --

00:04:24.634 --> 00:04:25.834
like, "Why is everyone
so quiet?"

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:28.267
Like, I literally
was not present

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:30.033
for that whole, entire moment.

00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:31.400
And as I'm walking to the stage,

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.701
I'm kind of putting
2 and 2 together

00:04:34.701 --> 00:04:39.534
and I realize that that
was a real moment like

00:04:39.534 --> 00:04:41.534
maybe three seconds
before I spoke words.

00:04:41.534 --> 00:04:44.000
But, in my mind, they're just
doing a sketch or whatever,

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.501
and I'm just like, "Okay, Ahmir.

00:04:45.501 --> 00:04:48.300
Remember to thank your mom,
your dad, thank..."

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.601
-Really?
-So I was not present at all.

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:52.567
I was just in a blank space.

00:04:52.567 --> 00:04:56.200
-And did people sitting
around you have a vibe, too?

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:57.634
-I was in the fun section.

00:04:57.634 --> 00:05:00.367
I was -- I was right -- Like,
I was in the documentary --

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:05.467
They put the documentary people
and the animation people,

00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:07.634
so the "Encanto" --
Like, that whole --

00:05:07.634 --> 00:05:12.934
They were having,
like, Hot Takis and Fritos.

00:05:12.934 --> 00:05:14.968
-How did they smuggle that
into the Oscars?

00:05:14.968 --> 00:05:17.133
-Dude, it -- We had a picnic.

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:21.300
Like, they were sharing,
like, snacks with me.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.234
-You looked great.
Your mom looked great.

00:05:23.234 --> 00:05:25.667
I want to show a picture
of you and your mom, just so --

00:05:25.667 --> 00:05:27.334
-You know, I've not --

00:05:27.334 --> 00:05:30.434
I purposely have not
watched the highlight reel,

00:05:30.434 --> 00:05:33.701
but I hear that --
My mom loves crying at anything.

00:05:33.701 --> 00:05:35.234
-Dude, I lost it.

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:37.300
-Like, my first-grade recital,
she cried.

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:39.133
Like, she always cries
at anything.

00:05:39.133 --> 00:05:41.334
Like, "Mom, I got a C-minus."

00:05:41.334 --> 00:05:43.100
"Oh, my baby!"
Like...

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:44.567
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.567 --> 00:05:46.000
-I just know her from sitting

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.667
right in the audience up there
and saying hi to her.

00:05:47.667 --> 00:05:49.133
-So, they did a close-up
of my mom?

00:05:49.133 --> 00:05:52.367
-Whew! Dude...
-Aw, man! I already know.

00:05:52.367 --> 00:05:55.267
-No, dude. I lost it, dude.
I was -- I lost it.

00:05:55.267 --> 00:05:56.634
Nancy, everyone.

00:05:56.634 --> 00:05:59.467
-I'm not one to go in the --
Like, I don't --

00:05:59.467 --> 00:06:01.100
This is an old reference,
but you know, like,

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:03.200
Al Bundy does the whole, like,
Polk High School,

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:05.334
four-touchdowns,
highlight-reel thing.

00:06:05.334 --> 00:06:06.367
-Yeah.

00:06:06.367 --> 00:06:09.167
-Ask your kids --
Ask your parents.

00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:14.868
But, you know, I've not watched
any highlight reel or anything.

00:06:14.868 --> 00:06:17.934
So I don't want to get stuck
in that thing where I'm like,

00:06:17.934 --> 00:06:19.067
"Just watch it.

00:06:19.067 --> 00:06:20.734
Okay, watch me walk
to the stage right now."

00:06:20.734 --> 00:06:22.067
-Yeah, yeah.

00:06:22.067 --> 00:06:23.434
I can't tell you -- Obviously,

00:06:23.434 --> 00:06:24.701
you know we love you
and we're proud of you,

00:06:24.701 --> 00:06:27.701
but everybody -- everybody --
who knows you

00:06:27.701 --> 00:06:29.434
loves you and is
so proud of you, dude.

00:06:29.434 --> 00:06:31.167
It couldn't have happened to
a better dude.

00:06:31.167 --> 00:06:32.400
-I'm gonna --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:34.300
Let me just tell you.

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:38.868
I'm gonna tell you, what's --
Just real quick.

00:06:38.868 --> 00:06:41.868
And I'm not world-famous for
deflecting any praise

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:46.267
or love or whatever, but I have
to say that, you know,

00:06:46.267 --> 00:06:52.167
my true reward in this
whole thing is that, you know,

00:06:52.167 --> 00:06:56.434
I'm in this creative atmosphere.

00:06:56.434 --> 00:06:59.200
Like, I consider this
30 Rock universe --

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:00.767
Like, I don't say like,
"Oh, I'm going to

00:07:00.767 --> 00:07:03.400
'The Tonight Show'
or 'Fallon' or what --"

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:06.434
30 Rock is, like, the
best college I've ever been to,

00:07:06.434 --> 00:07:07.701
where I can go to
different floors

00:07:07.701 --> 00:07:09.801
and watch people work,
and then they're creative.

00:07:09.801 --> 00:07:14.300
And the fact that I, like,
get to create with my friends

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:20.367
over there and with you,
that, to me, is the real --

00:07:20.367 --> 00:07:22.901
And I know it sounds like
so a Hollywood answer.

00:07:22.901 --> 00:07:24.434
Like, "Oh,
that's my real reward,"

00:07:24.434 --> 00:07:27.133
but that, to me,
is what matters.

00:07:27.133 --> 00:07:31.100
And the fact that I get to
live out my dreams,

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:34.567
and you provided
this platform for me to --

00:07:34.567 --> 00:07:37.267
if I want to write a cookbook
one day or if I want to,

00:07:37.267 --> 00:07:39.200
you know, teach class or
start a radio show.

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:43.234
And, like, I didn't even start
to listen to my dreams

00:07:43.234 --> 00:07:47.868
until I came here in 2009,
so I really want to thank you

00:07:47.868 --> 00:07:50.067
for giving me that platform.

00:07:50.067 --> 00:07:51.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:51.968 --> 00:07:53.801
-Academy Award-winning director
Questlove.

00:07:53.801 --> 00:07:55.167
-Thank you.

00:07:55.167 --> 00:07:58.968
-Academy Award-winning director
Questlove, everybody!

00:07:58.968 --> 00:08:01.801
Check out his Oscar-winning
documentary, "Summer of Soul,"

00:08:01.801 --> 00:08:02.801
on Hulu.

